---
/**
 * Terms of use for the website itself — not for client engagements, which
 * are governed by the written agreement signed for each one.
 *
 * Deliberately short and plain. It names no governing law or jurisdiction
 * because none has been supplied; have it reviewed and complete that before
 * relying on it (docs/claims-register.md → "Owner actions").
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '30 September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms for using the NYT Software Solutions website: what its content is and is not, links to client systems, trademarks, and acceptable use."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms of use' }]}
>
  <article class="container legal">
    <header class="legal-head">
      <p class="page-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">
        These terms cover your use of this website. They do not cover software
        projects: every engagement with {site.legalName} is governed by the
        written agreement signed for it.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        The site describes {site.name}, its services and its past work. It is
        information, not an offer. Nothing on it — including engagement
        descriptions, typical timelines and the Blueprint Studio — is a quote,
        a price or a commitment to deliver anything by a particular date. The
        Blueprint Studio produces an indicative shape and calendar from a few
        answers; real scope, cost and dates are set in a written estimate and
        agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Case studies and client systems</h2>
      <p>
        Case studies describe systems we designed and built for our clients.
        The systems, their names and their content belong to those clients.
        Links to live client systems are provided so you can see the work; we
        do not control those sites, and their own terms apply there. Figures
        in case studies are attributed to their source on the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Technology names and logos shown on this site belong to their owners
        and are used only to name the tools we work with. Their use does not
        imply endorsement or partnership.
      </p>

      <h2>Our content</h2>
      <p>
        Text, drawings and code on this site are © {site.legalName} unless
        stated otherwise. You are welcome to link to any page. Please ask before
        reusing content elsewhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site fairly</h2>
      <p>
        Please do not use the contact form to send spam or unlawful content, or
        try to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or the
        systems behind it. If you believe you have found a security issue,
        email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will look
        into it.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep the site accurate and available, but it is provided as
        it is, and to the extent the law allows we are not liable for losses
        arising from relying on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; the date at the top shows when they last
        changed. Questions to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Page>
